@page "/coding-agent"
@layout ShowroomLayout

@* The coding agent at work (F120; in the showroom since F127.1): a session recorded once, played back in its work
   window on the stage, what it shows beside it, then the offer. The live chat stays closed to visitors (FX88), so
   this is the door the header and the hero lead to. *@

<PageTitle>The coding agent · louis-agent</PageTitle>
<PageHead Description="Watch the louis-agent coding agent fix a real bug: it runs the tests, reads the code, fixes it on a branch and runs the tests again." />

<DemoStage Accent="TileAccent.Red" Kicker="Agents at work · The coding agent">
    <Title>Watch it fix a real bug.</Title>
    <Lede>
        A small invoice matcher, and bank payments that don't find their invoices. <span class="stage-made-up">This is
            the session as it happened, played back. Nothing runs while you watch. The live agent runs shell commands,
            so it runs only for its owner, behind a key.</span>
    </Lede>
    <Player>
        <RecordedChat Turns="Session" Title="the coding agent · toolsets: files, git, dotnet" PlayAgain="Play it again"
                      Currency="Rand">
            <Ending>
                <GuideButton Class="is-plain" Question="I watched the coding agent fix the invoice matcher. Could I get an agent like that for my team?">Ask the guide about one</GuideButton>
            </Ending>
        </RecordedChat>
    </Player>
    <Cues>
        <div class="work-notes">
            <h2 class="work-notes-heading">What it shows</h2>
            <ul class="work-notes-list">
                <li><strong>Every tool is a pack.</strong> It reads the files, runs the tests and writes the fix with the files, git and dotnet packs, the same ones it uses in Rider and the terminal.</li>
                <li><strong>It checks its own work.</strong> Two tests fail before the fix and all four pass after it, and it says which and why.</li>
                <li><strong>It leaves the commit to you.</strong> The fix sits in the working tree, and it says so.</li>
                <li><strong>It cost about R0.10.</strong> Seven requests on Claude Haiku, priced by the usage ledger, the bill under the answer.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </Cues>
    <Offer>
        <span>Want an agent like this on your own code?</span>
        <a href="/contact">Ask for yours →</a>
    </Offer>
</DemoStage>
